1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,580
1945. My dearest one, I have just heard the news that all the army men taking POW are

2
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:13,280
to return to their homes. Because of the shipping situation, we may not commence to go before

3
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:19,400
the end of February, but can probably count on being in England sometime in March. It

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:28,000
may be sooner. It has made me very warm inside. It's terrific. It's wonderful. Shattering.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,039
I don't know what to say and I cannot think. The delay is nothing. The decision is everything.

6
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:39,759
Now I am confirming in my head the little decisions I have made when contemplating just

7
00:00:39,759 --> 00:00:45,200
the possibility. I must spend the first days at home. I must see Deb and her mother. I

8
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:53,240
must consider giving a party somewhere. Above all, I must be with you. I must warm you,

9
00:00:53,240 --> 00:01:00,700
surround you, love you, and be kind to you. Tell me anything that's in your mind.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:11,840
mind, write tons and tons and tons and plan our time. I would prefer not to get married,

11
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:25,760
but want you to agree on the point. In the battle I was afraid for you, for my mother,

12
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:33,379
for myself. Wait, we must, my love and my darling. Let us meet, let us be, let us know,

13
00:01:33,379 --> 00:01:39,099
but do not let us now make any mistakes. I am anxious, very anxious, that you should

14
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:44,980
not misunderstand what I have said. Say what you think, but please agree and remember I

15
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:52,340
was afraid and I am still afraid. How good for us to see each other before I am completely

16
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:59,340
bald. If you find wisps of hair on the top of my head.

17
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:07,599
Not much good me trying to write about recent experiences now that I know I shall be able to tell you everything myself within such a short time.

18
00:02:07,959 --> 00:02:14,419
What I have my eye on now is the first letter from you saying that you know I am alright and then next saying you know I am coming to you.

19
00:02:15,539 --> 00:02:19,500
Must try and keep out of hospital with some of these post-POW complaints.

20
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:23,319
Plan a week somewhere, not Boscombe or Bournemouth, and think of being together.

21
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,939
The glory of you.

22
00:02:25,939 --> 00:02:31,939
When I was captive I used to try and contact you and think hard.

23
00:02:32,639 --> 00:02:36,120
Bessie, my dearest, I am alright. Do not worry.

24
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:45,439
I never thought that I would get through somehow, but now it's over and you know that I am alright and going to be with you soon to join and enjoy.

25
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:49,020
Do not get very excited outwardly.

26
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:54,180
I am conscious of the inner tumult, the clamour, but I am not too much outwardly joyful.

27
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:57,360
Moderation is my advice. Watch the buses as you cross the streets.

28
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,360
LAUGHTER

29
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:58,879
LAUGHTER

30
00:02:58,879 --> 00:02:59,520
travelling

31
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,219
Ooooh...

32
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:00,560
LAUGHTER

33
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:06,060
..

34
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,319
We're free of duties and yesterday I went to our friends in Athens taking some of your

35
00:03:05,319 --> 00:03:08,000
coffee and cocoa which they were very pleased to have.

36
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,719
Thank you for sending it.

37
00:03:09,719 --> 00:03:15,500
We were embraced very excitedly, kissing and so on continental fashion.

38
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:24,699
I hope that you will not start buying any clothes if you have any coupons left because

39
00:03:24,699 --> 00:03:27,759
you think you must look nice for me.

40
00:03:27,759 --> 00:03:29,240
I shall be sorry if you do.

41
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:33,159
Just carry on as near as possible to normal.

42
00:03:33,159 --> 00:03:38,460
My return at the present time allows us to make public our mutual attachment.

43
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:44,159
I shall tell my family that I hope to spend a week away with you somewhere during my leave.

44
00:03:44,159 --> 00:03:48,920
My counsel to you is to tell as few people as possible.

45
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:52,639
To someone like Miss Ferguson you can politely reply to observations that you thought it

46
00:03:52,639 --> 00:03:56,639
was your business rather than hers.

47
00:03:56,639 --> 00:03:58,740
Try to avoid preening yourself and saying much.

48
00:03:58,740 --> 00:03:59,740
This is my advice.

49
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:00,659
This is my advice.

50
00:04:00,659 --> 00:04:02,659
This is my advice.

51
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,460
Not anything but that.

52
00:04:02,699 --> 00:04:03,840
I hope you understand.

53
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:08,639
I do not ever want it to be anything but our affair.

54
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:11,800
Do not permit any intrusion.

55
00:04:14,319 --> 00:04:17,079
I do not know how long leave I shall get.

56
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:18,939
I could get as little as 14 days

57
00:04:18,939 --> 00:04:20,639
and I may get as much as a month.

58
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:25,540
I'm wondering how I shall tell you that I am in England.

59
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:26,500
Probably it will still be quicker

60
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,040
to send a telegram than a letter

61
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,399
and I hope to send you one

62
00:04:29,399 --> 00:04:31,519
announcing that I am on the same island.

63
00:04:31,519 --> 00:04:33,120
I will send another when I'm actually soon

64
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,420
to get on the London-bound train

65
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:36,720
and you can ring Lee Green 0509

66
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:38,439
when you think I have arrived there.

67
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,199
You must bear in mind that I shall be with my brother

68
00:04:42,199 --> 00:04:43,899
until we get home.

69
00:04:43,899 --> 00:04:46,579
Also that having been away from home for so long

70
00:04:46,579 --> 00:04:49,060
my parents will want to see a lot of me.

71
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:52,819
I hope that everything will work itself out

72
00:04:52,819 --> 00:04:55,019
without any unhappiness to anyone.

73
00:04:56,379 --> 00:04:58,120
I shall be in great demand from two or three points

74
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,819
and it will be difficult to manage without a fence.

75
00:04:59,819 --> 00:05:29,800
Let's go.

76
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:10,680
Strange thing, but I cannot seem to get going and write very freely.

77
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:13,819
All I'm thinking about is I am going home.

78
00:05:13,819 --> 00:05:16,600
I'm going to see her.

79
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:23,800
It's a fact, a real thing, an impending event like Trove Tuesday, Christmas Day, or the

80
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,519
Lord Mayor's banquet.

81
00:05:25,519 --> 00:05:32,920
You have to be abroad, you have to be really, truly, hermetically sealed off from your intimates,

82
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:40,980
from your home to realise what a gift this going home is.

83
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:45,439
The few letters of yours that I had on me, I burnt the day previous to our surrender,

84
00:05:45,439 --> 00:05:48,079
so no one but myself has read your words.

85
00:05:48,079 --> 00:05:52,480
In the first ten days of our captivity, I did not think any soft thoughts about you.

86
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:57,860
All I did was concentrate on trying to tell you I was alright.

87
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,860
But when we had a few supplies dropped by aircraft...

88
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:00,860
...

89
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,860
...

90
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:02,860
...

91
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:03,860
...

92
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:04,860
...

93
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:05,860
...

94
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:07,860
...

95
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:09,860
...

96
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:11,860
...

97
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:13,860
...

98
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:15,860
...

99
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:04,560
great risk to themselves in the misty snowbound Greek mountain villages and we started hoping

100
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:09,759
we might get sent home upon our release. I was always wondering about you, about us.

101
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:15,439
It is a pity that the winter weather will not be kind to us out of doors.

102
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:20,160
It would be nice sitting next to you in the pictures, no matter what may be on the screen.

103
00:06:21,279 --> 00:06:24,800
It would be grand to know that we have each other's support and sympathy.

104
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:30,240
Wouldn't it be wonderful to be together, really together?

